2026-09-28 — T05k: stop silently following the ambient Rust stable toolchain.

RED: the host's active stable alias resolves to Rust/Clippy 1.98.0 (88d9e12ae),
while contracts/build-environment.json freezes 1.97.1 (8bab26f4f). No repository
toolchain file existed. The changed gate also scheduled no packages for either
rust-toolchain spelling. Thirteen targeted tests produce five failing assertions:
the missing pin plus committed/uncommitted changes of each toolchain filename.

Fix: rust-toolchain.toml selects the already installed 1.97.1 with Clippy and
rustfmt. The existing changed gate treats either toolchain filename as a full
workspace change, just as Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock. This is not a change to the
frozen compiler version and does not change the host's global default toolchain.
README distinguishes CARGO_BUILD_JOBS (all Cargo invocations) from test-only -j.

The actual installed rustc and cargo match the frozen contract hashes:
rustc 210df6794001b73ec3d453878707fa1e0bdcb63c427024a6e6574bbe5615a4da
cargo 7672ead309d505577c018fff2cafb3433601f073e38cbe87359ac1f7b944bbf5

GREEN under Rust/Cargo 1.97.1, Clippy 0.1.97 and its rustfmt:
* All 17 workspace crates: 2801 PASS / 0 FAIL / 4 historical ignored.
* Clippy --all-targets -D warnings and workspace fmt check PASS.
* All 315 ladder Python tests PASS, including the thirteen targeted gate tests.
* Ruff tools/tests-acceptance PASS; status renderer --check PASS.
* Fresh layout observations: 128/128 + 22/22 PASS against the unchanged frozen
  oracle manifests. No new reference-layout execution is claimed.
* Textual grammar: 54 renderer / 54 specified shapes, zero differences. This
  is shape coverage, not a proof that the full spec is implemented.
* Fresh empty-CARGO_HOME, vendored --locked --offline replay: thirteen tests
  PASS, zero failure/ignore, using the existing pinned-check target.
* All six logical-immediate fixture variants produce byte-identical assembly
  with the 1.97.1 compiler and the previously native-tested 1.98.0 compiler.
  Native execution is not re-labelled as a new independent measurement.

Resource policy: target/pinned-check, CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0,
CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=0, CARGO_PROFILE_TEST_DEBUG=0, CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true.
The cache is 2.8 GiB at the first complete build, not another source/workspace or
VM clone. No running kernel compiler or kernel object was changed.

Important boundary: frozen kernel compiler 65035621f0921b11033455a2d02e72f94481fd6d3b82468279645a7a1e1fb3e5
contains /rustc/88d9e12ae178fab0fb5cc050a94da85685d449ea, the 1.98.0 standard
library source marker. It is NOT re-labelled as a 1.97.1 build. Its ongoing
7002-object composition keeps its actual compiler identity. A future final
campaign must use an explicitly recorded pinned build; this pin does not
retroactively certify previous builds or close T04/B10/K13/K14/T05.

